===Etymology 2===
Origin unknown. Perhaps from ''The Dong with a Luminous Nose'', an 1894 poem by {{w|Edward Lear}} about a mythical creature. Attested since the 1930s.

====Noun====
{{en-noun}}

# {{lb|en|slang}} A [[penis]].
#* {{quote-book|en|1969|Philip Roth|Portnoy’s Complaint||18|Nevertheless, I was wholly incapable of keeping my paws from my '''dong''' once it started the climb up my belly.}}
#* '''1983''', "Penis Song" (from ''{{w|Monty Python's The Meaning of Life}}'')
#*: Isn't it awfully nice to have a penis?<br>Isn't it frightfully good to have a '''dong'''?
# {{lb|en|slang|by extension}} A [[dildo]], specifically a [[synthetic]] [[anatomical]] [[replica]] of the penis.

